.Dd November 5, 2026
.Dt XBPRETTY.CONF 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm xbpretty.conf
.Nd configuration file for xbpretty
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Pa /etc/xbpretty/config.toml
.Pa ~/.config/xbpretty/config.toml
.Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/xbpretty/config.toml
.Pa FILE
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is an optional TOML configuration file for
xbpretty(8).
It uses nala's schema: the [Nala], [Ui], [Color] and [Color.theme] tables plus
the xbps-only [Xbps] table.
Every key is optional.
Missing files and missing keys resolve to the built-in defaults, and
command-line flags override configuration values.
.Pp
A rev 6 run never writes, rewrites, converts or backs up a configuration file.
It writes no marker and no cache.
Configuration warnings never change the command's exit status.
.Sh LAYERS
Layers are read in this order; later layers win per key, and theme styles
merge role by role.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It system layer
/etc/xbpretty/config.toml, optional and absent by default.
The package never creates this file or its directory.
.It user layer
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/xbpretty/config.toml when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is absolute, else
~/.config/xbpretty/config.toml.
Under sudo or doas the invoking user's passwd home is used and XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is ignored.
.It Cm --config Ar FILE
A long-only global option that replaces both default layers for the run.
It is accepted before or after the subcommand.
The short form -c is fetch's --country and is a usage error on every other
command.
.El
Each existing layer is parsed and validated independently.
A missing default layer is silent; an existing unreadable or invalid layer is
a hard error and exits 2.
A missing explicit --config file is also a hard error.
XBPRETTY_CONFIG is not supported.
.Sh KEYS
.Ss Nala
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm auto_remove
Plan and offer the implicit orphan removal after a successful transaction.
Default: true.
.It Cm auto_update
Refresh the repository index before the upgrade family.
Default: true.
.It Cm update_show_packages
With update, list each upgradable package instead of only the count.
Default: false.
.It Cm full_upgrade
Accepted compatibility switch; xbps -u never removes packages.
Default: false.
.It Cm simple
Use the one-line-per-operation simple summary.
Default: false.
.It Cm assume_yes
Skip the confirmation prompt, as -y does.
Default: false.
.El
.Ss Ui
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm mode
Interface mode: Auto, Plain or Tui.
Default: "Auto".
.It Cm unit
Size unit: Binary or Decimal.
Default: "Binary".
.El
.Ss Color
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm mode
Colour mode: Auto, Always or Never.
Default: "Auto".
.El
.Ss Color.theme
Each theme role is an inline table of the form { fg = "BrightGreen" },
optionally with bg and modifier.
An omitted modifier means bold; an empty modifier means none.
The nine roles are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm Primary
Section rules, labels and headings.
.It Cm Secondary
Secondary labels.
.It Cm Highlight
Package names and highlighted values.
.It Cm Regular
Regular body text.
.It Cm ProgressFilled
Filled part of the progress bar.
.It Cm ProgressUnfilled
Unfilled part of the progress bar.
.It Cm Notice
Notices and version highlights.
.It Cm Warning
Warnings.
.It Cm Error
Errors.
.El
.Ss Xbps
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm install_path
Path to xbps-install; privileged and trust-gated under root.
Default: "xbps-install".
.It Cm remove_path
Path to xbps-remove; privileged and trust-gated under root.
Default: "xbps-remove".
.It Cm query_path
Path to xbps-query; privileged and trust-gated under root.
Default: "xbps-query".
.It Cm rindex_path
Path to xbps-rindex; privileged and trust-gated under root.
Default: "xbps-rindex".
.It Cm uhelper_path
Path to xbps-uhelper; privileged and trust-gated under root.
Default: "xbps-uhelper".
.It Cm pkgdb_path
Path to xbps-pkgdb; privileged and trust-gated under root.
Default: "xbps-pkgdb".
.It Cm transaction_log
Append a line to the transaction log after a successful run.
Default: true.
.El
.Sh VALUES
.Ss Colours
A colour is a named ANSI colour, an indexed colour 0-255, or an RGB triplet.
Named colours are Reset, Black, Red, Green, Yellow, Blue, Magenta, Cyan, Gray,
DarkGray, LightRed, LightGreen, LightYellow, LightBlue, LightMagenta,
LightCyan and White.
Indexed colours use an integer; RGB colours use rgb(r, g, b).
.Ss Modifiers
The accepted modifiers are bold, dim, italic, underlined, slow_blink,
rapid_blink, reversed, hidden and crossed_out.
.Ss Enumerations
[Ui] mode is Auto, Plain or Tui; [Ui] unit is Binary or Decimal; [Color] mode
is Auto, Always or Never.
Values are case-sensitive.
.Sh LEGACY KEYS
Rev 6 accepts ten rev-5 top-level flat keys before the first table header.
They are mapped where possible and never rewritten.
Alias keys warn once per key; the three retired keys warn and are ignored.
All legacy keys are removed in rev 7, where they become unknown keys and exit
2.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm assume_yes
Rename to [Nala] assume_yes.
.It Cm sync
Rename to [Nala] auto_update.
.It Cm log
Rename to [Xbps] transaction_log.
.It Cm xbps_install_path
Rename to [Xbps] install_path.
.It Cm xbps_remove_path
Rename to [Xbps] remove_path.
.It Cm xbps_query_path
Rename to [Xbps] query_path.
.It Cm color
Rename to [Color] mode and map auto/always/never to Auto/Always/Never.
.It Cm verbose
Retired; pass -v on the command line.
.It Cm box_style
Retired; the summary has no box.
.It Cm progress_bar
Retired; use [Ui] mode = "Plain".
.El
Within a file the canonical key wins.
Across layers the later layer wins regardless of spelling.
Rev 6 also accepts rev-5 value forms for the ten legacy keys only: quoted
booleans and bare strings at top level.
Everything else remains strict TOML, and duplicate keys are an error.
.Pp
When any legacy key is seen, one aggregate warning is printed once per run.
--debug adds one line per legacy key and a summary.
Warnings never change the exit code.
.Sh TRUST
When effective UID is 0, a [Xbps] path key is honoured only if the supplying
layer is a regular file owned by UID 0 with no group or world write
permission.
The check reads owner, mode and regular-file status from the same opened
descriptor that supplies the contents, so a path swap cannot defeat it.
Symlinks are followed and judged on the target inode.
.Pp
An untrusted path key is ignored, never executed, and produces one warning
naming the path, the key and the observed owner and mode.
Non-privileged keys from the same layer still apply.
The system layer is not automatically trusted.
A legacy xbps_*_path key is gated identically after alias resolution.
Non-root runs honour every layer.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm 0
The configuration parsed and the command ran successfully.
.It Cm 2
An existing layer is unreadable, invalid TOML, contains an unknown key,
contains an out-of-range value, or an explicit --config file is missing.
.El
An xbps child's exit status is passed through unchanged.
.Sh SECURITY
The package installs no file under /etc, creates no /etc/xbpretty directory,
and has no conf_files entry.
The system layer is optional and administrator-created.
Do not make a privileged configuration layer group- or world-writable: its
[Xbps] binary paths are ignored under root.
.Pp
The file is parsed as a strict TOML subset.
It cannot execute code, include another file, or fetch remote content.
xbpretty never writes the file, so a successful run leaves the administrator's
or user's contents byte-identical.
.Sh SEE ALSO
xbpretty(8)
.Pp
https://github.com/soubarnak/xbpretty
